  "implementation": {
    "ownership": "The existing per-device submission queue owns a completion epoch and condition variable. Native work drains, captures retire and completion status publishes before queue bookkeeping advances the epoch and notifies all public waiters.",
    "no_lost_wake": "Observe epoch before checking fence/timeline predicates, then wait under the same queue mutex only while the epoch is unchanged. Completion before blocking is retained; unrelated wakes recheck the original deadline and predicates.",
    "timeout": "Zero-time polls retain status/error ordering. Finite calls use one steady-clock deadline; unsigned durations outside the representable clock range saturate without signed overflow. Infinite calls block on notification without timed polling.",
    "preserved": "Queue admission, command execution, error handling, native drains, handle checks, timeline ordering, reset/resource lifetime and worker readiness scheduling remain unchanged. No busy-spin loop, global timer/power policy or per-kernel synchronization is added."
  },
  "clean_release_tests": {
    "total": 146,
